 "article": {
  "title": "The Cost of Convenience: Return Fees",
  "topic": "消费与电商（退货费用）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 160,
  "paras": [
   "Free returns were once a promise that convinced shoppers to click. Now they are a line item that retailers are quietly deleting.",
   "Returning a parcel is not free, even when the customer pays nothing. Someone sorts it, inspects it, repackages it, and often sells it at a discount. In fashion, the true cost can reach a third of the item's price, and a large share of returned clothes end up shredded or shipped abroad.",
   "Retailers have tried three approaches. Some charge a small fee, which cuts impulse buying. Some keep returns free but lengthen delivery. A few use software that flags serial returners and quietly restricts them, a practice that has already produced lawsuits.",
   "The consumer's interest is not obvious. A fee punishes the customer who ordered two sizes because the sizing chart was wrong. The better fix is upstream: accurate photographs, honest measurements and fewer, better-made items. Convenience that is paid for by the planet is not really convenient."
  ],
  "zh": "“免费退货”曾经是让顾客下单的承诺，如今成了零售商悄悄删掉的一行成本。退一个包裹并不免费，即使顾客一分钱不付：总有人要分拣、检查、重新包装，最后往往打折卖掉。在服装品类，真实退货成本可达商品价的三分之一，相当一部分退回的衣服被切碎或运往海外。零售商试过三种做法：收一点费用，抑制冲动购买；保持免费但拉长配送；或者用软件标记“惯犯”并悄悄限制，这已经引发诉讼。消费者的利益并不显然：收费惩罚的是因为尺码表出错而买了两个码的顾客。更好的办法在上游——准确的照片、诚实的尺寸、更少但做得更好的商品。由地球来买单的便利，其实并不便利。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "A fee punishes the customer who ordered two sizes because the sizing chart was wrong.",
    "cn": "收费惩罚的是那位因为尺码表有误而买了两个码的顾客。",
    "why": "who 定语从句修饰 customer，because 从句说明原因；注意 because 修饰的是 ordered 而不是 punishes，读句要看逻辑归属。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Convenience that is paid for by the planet is not really convenient.",
    "cn": "由地球来买单的便利，其实并不便利。",
    "why": "that 定语从句修饰 Convenience，be paid for by 用被动表示“由……承担代价”；句末 convenient 回扣主语形成反讽，是很好的收尾句。"
   }
  ],
